I cannot honestly cite an upstream commit hash or series: this environment gives me only `rtk` (grep over the working tree) — no git history, no network, no `Documentation`/changelog with that information. Any hash I produced would be fabricated. What I can say with confidence is that the fix must land in `drivers/usb/typec/class.c` and take one of these shapes (all consistent with how upstream has fixed the sibling races here):

1. Track link state per USB device (e.g. a bitfield/flag set only after both `sysfs_create_link()` calls succeed) and skip `typec_partner_unlink_device()` otherwise.
2. Take a reference: `get_device()` in `typec_partner_attach()`, `put_device()` in `typec_partner_deattach()`/`typec_unregister_partner()`.
3. Guard the removal: `if (dev->kobj.sd)` / `device_is_registered(dev)` before `sysfs_remove_link(&dev->kobj, "typec")`.

